but an outcast and a loser.

261
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,734
He used to be nothing
but an outcast and a loser.

262
00:21:59,735 --> 00:22:03,989
An outcast and a loser.

263
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,243
"Outcast"?

264
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:10,746
"Loser"?

265
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:16,961
There she goes again.
Let's go stop her.

266
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:26,387
I bet
people can't even imagine his past.

267
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:38,565
- Was it you?
- Excuse me?

268
00:22:38,566 --> 00:22:41,652
You were the one bullying
and isolating him

269
00:22:42,278 --> 00:22:43,279
weren't you?

270
00:22:43,821 --> 00:22:48,492
I'm never going to forgive you!

271
00:23:09,597 --> 00:23:10,723
Your nose is bleeding.

272
00:23:15,311 --> 00:23:16,729
We're sorry.

273
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:18,647
We're so sorry.

274
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:22,526
My friend has been having
such a hard time finding a job

275
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:25,111
- and life has been so rough
- You did well.

276
00:23:25,112 --> 00:23:27,655
that she ended up developing
anger management issues.

277
00:23:27,656 --> 00:23:29,407
We're truly sorry.

278
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:30,993
We're so, truly sorry.

279
00:23:31,243 --> 00:23:34,204
What are you apologizing for?
I'm not sorry at all.

280
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,499
Bullying is the worst.

281
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,252
Do you even know what that's like?

282
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:47,384
I'm sorry.

283
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:50,638
You don't, do you?

284
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:04,693
- Jeez.
- What are they doing?

285
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:06,195
- What the...
- Did he hit her?

286
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:23,920
My friend is so deeply apologetic
that she's on her knees.

287
00:24:23,921 --> 00:24:25,756
I guess she's reflecting
on her actions a lot, right?

288
00:24:26,340 --> 00:24:27,466
Right?

289
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:30,636
Well...

290
00:24:31,512 --> 00:24:32,763
That's enough. Just leave.

291
00:24:33,472 --> 00:24:35,264
How generous of you.

292
00:24:35,265 --> 00:24:37,141
Bless you. Thank you.

293
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:38,560
Thank you.

294
00:24:39,395 --> 00:24:40,561
Bye.

295
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:42,940
Right?

296
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:45,651
- Hey, let go of me!
- Knock it off.

297
00:24:45,985 --> 00:24:47,027
What?

298
00:24:47,486 --> 00:24:49,613
She got anger management issues
because she couldn't get a job?

299
00:24:51,198 --> 00:24:52,533
For someone who works at SE.

300
00:24:52,908 --> 00:24:54,034
Do you know her?

301
00:24:56,328 --> 00:24:57,538
She's a stranger.

302
00:24:58,288 --> 00:24:59,289
Exactly.

303
00:25:00,082 --> 00:25:01,250
I should've asked for her number.

304
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:03,210
Hurry up.

305
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:05,379
Jeez, wait.

306
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:08,799
- Throw her.
- Throw her.

307
00:25:13,429 --> 00:25:14,555
Oh, man.

308
00:25:14,972 --> 00:25:16,015
It's like

309
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:18,516
her weight literally doubled
the second she got drunk.

310
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:19,601
Darn it.

311
00:25:23,439 --> 00:25:24,898
This is nuts.

312
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:28,151
FOREVER LEE CHAN

313
00:25:28,152 --> 00:25:31,155
Goodness. Anyway,
I guess Da-reum really is

314
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:33,741
living out the ultimate
successful fan.

315
00:25:35,117 --> 00:25:36,493
I wonder if Chan even knows

316
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:39,037
that he still has such a die-hard fan

317
00:25:39,038 --> 00:25:40,914
when D.N.X disbanded a decade ago.

318
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:43,125
Beats me.

319
00:25:44,334 --> 00:25:46,503
Hey, let's go home.

320
00:25:48,714 --> 00:25:49,965
Oh, wait.

321
00:25:53,469 --> 00:25:54,595
Come on, let's go.

322
00:26:43,143 --> 00:26:45,270
SUNGJU STATION

323
00:26:50,984 --> 00:26:52,111
SUNGJU STATION

324
00:27:39,074 --> 00:27:41,659
Which department are you in?

325
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:43,704
I'm with the Merchandising Team.

326
00:27:44,580 --> 00:27:46,330
I'm in Marketing.

327
00:27:46,331 --> 00:27:47,915
Marketing? Me too.

328
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:50,251
- Really?
- I hope we get along.

329
00:27:50,252 --> 00:27:52,211
My name is Park Young-woo.

330
00:27:52,212 --> 00:27:53,379
What are your names?

331
00:27:53,380 --> 00:27:56,257
My name is Lee Min-a.

332
00:27:56,258 --> 00:27:57,425
- Lee Min-a.
- Lee Min-a.

333
00:27:57,426 --> 00:27:58,926
My name is Nam Da-reum.

334
00:27:58,927 --> 00:28:01,637
- Nam Da-reum. Lee Min-a and Da-reum.
- Nam Da-reum.

335
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:02,890
I see.

336
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,434
Let's get along.

337
00:28:05,726 --> 00:28:08,019
You know they say
loyalty to your batchmates is key.

338
00:28:08,020 --> 00:28:09,605
- How about a fist bump?
- Sure.

339
00:28:10,898 --> 00:28:12,441
You guys became close already?

340
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:18,196
Congratulations
on joining the Appello family.

341
00:28:18,197 --> 00:28:19,865
I'm Kim Mi-young

342
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:23,577
the Marketing Team Manager.
I'll be running today's orientation.

343
00:28:24,620 --> 00:28:26,663
Here are your employee ID cards.

344
00:28:27,956 --> 00:28:29,999
- Mr. Young-woo.
- Thank you.

345
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:31,627
- Ms. Min-a.
- Thank you.

346
00:28:31,835 --> 00:28:33,212
And Ms. Da-reum.

347
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:37,007
Thank you.

348
00:28:37,507 --> 00:28:40,259
Appello currently has 82 employees

349
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:42,303
plus three new hires joining today.

350
00:28:42,304 --> 00:28:45,348
That means this ID card is basically
Chan's limited-edition merch

351
00:28:45,349 --> 00:28:48,060
with only 85 of them
in the whole world.

352
00:28:48,852 --> 00:28:51,521
It's even customized!

353
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:55,692
All right, then. Let's dive
into the official company overview.

354
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:57,610
- Shall we?
- Yes, ma'am.

355
00:28:57,611 --> 00:28:58,612
This way.

356
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,492
- Come this way.
- Yes, ma'am.

357
00:29:11,041 --> 00:29:12,334
They come in different colors...

358
00:29:14,044 --> 00:29:15,295
Ms. Min-a.

359
00:29:17,297 --> 00:29:20,549
Most of Appello's partner brands
are centered online

360
00:29:20,550 --> 00:29:23,970
we host pop-up spaces on floor one
so they can meet customers in person.

361
00:29:23,971 --> 00:29:25,013
It's all right.

362
00:29:25,847 --> 00:29:28,266
We also offer spaces for our brands

363
00:29:28,267 --> 00:29:30,560
such as sewing rooms,
pattern rooms, and studios.

364
00:29:31,311 --> 00:29:34,397
As you can see,
our dress code is completely free.

365
00:29:34,398 --> 00:29:36,857
From tomorrow on, you can wear
a swimsuit, party clothes

366
00:29:36,858 --> 00:29:38,193
or anything that fits your style.

367
00:29:47,661 --> 00:29:50,414
This is the studio
for lookbook and campaign shoots.

368
00:29:51,039 --> 00:29:53,458
All of Appello's visual content is
basically born right here.

369
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:14,396
NAM DA-REUM

370
00:30:14,896 --> 00:30:18,567
On the fourth floor, we have
Marketing and Merchandising Teams.

371
00:30:20,652 --> 00:30:22,529
Oh, and the CEO's Office.

372
00:30:26,241 --> 00:30:29,535
All right. For our final stop,
let's go meet the CEO.

373
00:30:29,536 --> 00:30:31,872
- What, right now?
- Yes.

374
00:30:47,054 --> 00:30:49,806
Hello, I'm the new hire, Nam Da-reum.

375
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:51,975
Too cheesy.

376
00:30:55,270 --> 00:30:57,438
Nice to meet you. I'm Nam Da-reum.

377
00:30:57,439 --> 00:30:58,732
"I'm Nam Da-reum."

378
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:00,734
You sound like a call center agent.

379
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:03,570
Just act normal.

380
00:31:03,820 --> 00:31:05,197
And don't freeze up in front of Chan.

381
00:31:07,115 --> 00:31:08,700
Here, a secret weapon.

382
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:15,374
Take this calming pill,
and it will help with your nerves.

383
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:17,959
The calming pill.

384
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:34,976
Mr. Kang.

385
00:31:36,603 --> 00:31:38,480
They are our new recruits.

386
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:47,489
- It's nice to meet you.
- I'm new! I mean I'm Park Young-woo.

387
00:31:49,491 --> 00:31:50,616
It's nice to meet you.

388
00:31:50,617 --> 00:31:54,371
Hello, I'm the new hire, Lee Min-a.

389
00:32:04,256 --> 00:32:05,382
It's nice to meet you.

390
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:26,361
Is that you, Chan?

391
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:36,955
What the? Why is it someone else?

392
00:32:41,376 --> 00:32:42,794
I'm Nam Da-reum.

393
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:45,255
NAM DA-REUM

394
00:32:49,551 --> 00:32:51,635
Welcome to Appello.

395
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:54,473
My door is always open,
so feel free to drop by anytime.

396
00:32:55,140 --> 00:32:57,726
Don't feel too intimidated,
and just treat me as a coworker.

397
00:32:58,643 --> 00:33:00,479
Let's do some great work together.

398
00:33:01,021 --> 00:33:02,063
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

399
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:05,192
All right. Shall we wrap up here
and head out?

400
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,527
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

401
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:15,702
It's Chan.

402
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:32,677
Ms. Nam.

403
00:33:38,517 --> 00:33:39,975
Ms. Da-reum? What's wrong?

404
00:33:39,976 --> 00:33:42,646
- Are you okay? Try to breathe.
- Ms. Da-reum.

405
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:44,396
- Please call 911.
- Breathe.

406
00:33:44,397 --> 00:33:46,148
- What is it?
- Is something stuck in her throat?

407
00:33:46,149 --> 00:33:47,942
- You can't breathe?
- What's wrong?

408
00:33:47,943 --> 00:33:48,985
- Goodness.
- Breathe.

409
00:33:49,110 --> 00:33:50,570
Try to breathe.

410
00:34:24,688 --> 00:34:25,730
Da-reum...

411
00:34:26,398 --> 00:34:27,691
Are you okay?

412
00:34:28,233 --> 00:34:29,442
She should be fine now.

413
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:31,403
I'm not sure
what was choking her, though.

414
00:34:33,947 --> 00:34:35,114
- What...
- What's that?

415
00:34:35,115 --> 00:34:36,199
What is this?

416
00:34:57,262 --> 00:34:58,388
Oh, what's up?

417
00:34:58,722 --> 00:35:00,639
Listen up, everyone.
I've got big news.

418
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:01,890
Did you guys hear?

419
00:35:01,891 --> 00:35:05,270
A new recruit named Nam Da-reum
made big trouble from day one.

420
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:08,356
I mean, where is the discipline
in new recruits these days?

421
00:35:10,734 --> 00:35:11,776
What?

422
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:18,700
Mr. Lee Jin-sang.

423
00:35:22,746 --> 00:35:23,830
Oops.

424
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:25,498
My mistake.

425
00:35:28,627 --> 00:35:29,628
Go on.

426
00:35:33,965 --> 00:35:36,885
I threw up on Director Lee's pants
at my first company dinner.

427
00:35:39,888 --> 00:35:42,140
Anyone can make a mistake
when they're nervous.

428
00:35:42,641 --> 00:35:43,892
Don't worry about it.

429
00:35:46,061 --> 00:35:48,813
Thank you, Ms. Kim.

430
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:54,110
Excuse me.

431
00:35:54,694 --> 00:35:58,448
But wasn't Mr. Lee Chan the CEO?

432
00:35:58,948 --> 00:36:01,533
The two were previously co-CEOs

433
00:36:01,534 --> 00:36:03,912
but recently, the system changed
and we now have one CEO.

434
00:36:04,788 --> 00:36:07,915
- Then...
- Director Lee is only in charge

435
00:36:07,916 --> 00:36:09,584
of the fashion
for Appello's key events.

436
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:14,589
I see.

437
00:36:26,476 --> 00:36:28,143
What was it like
to finally see him in person?

438
00:36:28,144 --> 00:36:29,312
Did you manage to stay composed?

439
00:36:30,021 --> 00:36:33,482
A tear emoji? You must've cried.
Were you that moved?

440
00:36:33,483 --> 00:36:35,567
Let's throw a party
to remember your "made-it" moment.

441
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:37,277
- What do you want to eat?
- I'm in!

442
00:36:37,278 --> 00:36:39,238
Let's eat
whatever Namda wants to eat today.

443
00:36:39,239 --> 00:36:40,656
- I'm in!
- I'm in!

444
00:36:40,657 --> 00:36:42,117
- We're in!
- We're in!

445
00:36:43,535 --> 00:36:46,663
Girls, this is Chan's company

446
00:36:47,080 --> 00:36:48,790
but he's not around.

447
00:36:50,083 --> 00:36:52,167
That's like saying
there are no pads in push-up bras.

448
00:36:52,168 --> 00:36:53,837
That one has 4cm pads.

449
00:36:54,587 --> 00:36:56,296
- It's thick.
- Right. Sure.

450
00:36:56,297 --> 00:36:58,383
I'll take this in all colors.

451
00:36:58,717 --> 00:36:59,843
On top of that

452
00:37:00,969 --> 00:37:03,762
I ended up in our CEO's arms
on my first day.

453
00:37:03,763 --> 00:37:04,806
What?

454
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:08,476
What kind
of crazy development is this?

455
00:37:10,645 --> 00:37:13,106
I'm done for!

456
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:27,244
So the one
who slammed her face into your chest

457
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:28,329
was Ms. Nam Da-reum?

458
00:37:29,664 --> 00:37:33,293
She's from SE Corporation
of all places.

459
00:37:33,585 --> 00:37:34,878
Something doesn't feel right.

460
00:37:35,378 --> 00:37:37,629
If she had put it on her resume,
I wouldn't have hired her.

461
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:38,923
COMPUTER SKILLS LEVEL 1,
SURVEY ANALYST LEVEL 2...

462
00:37:39,424 --> 00:37:41,801
I don't see a reason
why she wants to work at Appello.

463
00:37:44,846 --> 00:37:46,598
Mr. Kang, do you think

464
00:37:46,806 --> 00:37:49,017
she could be a corporate spy
working with Director Kim?

465
00:37:50,268 --> 00:37:52,186
I looked into it and found out that

466
00:37:52,187 --> 00:37:55,440
he has infiltrated a few businesses
with spies to take them over.

467
00:37:58,359 --> 00:38:00,820
Let's keep
a close eye on her for a while.

468
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:17,253
In a way, Appello is quite smart.

469
00:38:17,629 --> 00:38:20,088
Everyone is busy
trying to snatch famous designers

470
00:38:20,089 --> 00:38:21,633
but you're going after new ones.

471
00:38:22,842 --> 00:38:24,093
It was Director Lee's idea.

472
00:38:24,552 --> 00:38:26,136
He was sad to see
talented brands disappear

473
00:38:26,137 --> 00:38:28,972
due to their lack of network
in distribution.

474
00:38:28,973 --> 00:38:31,059
Have you two always known each other?

475
00:38:31,351 --> 00:38:32,519
We went to high school together.

476
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:34,437
Oh, you two must be best friends.

477
00:38:35,355 --> 00:38:36,856
That's why
he left the business with you.

478
00:38:45,824 --> 00:38:48,116
Goodness. I look forward
to working with you.

479
00:38:48,117 --> 00:38:50,870
SE Corporation is now taking part
in the e-commerce industry.

480
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:53,456
We plan to open up
a fashion platform very soon.

481
00:38:53,748 --> 00:38:56,793
Wait, does that mean
you're competing against Appello?

482
00:38:57,460 --> 00:38:59,170
Compete? Hardly.

483
00:38:59,671 --> 00:39:01,464
We need to be similar in size
for that to happen.

484
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:05,175
Wouldn't it be weirder
if we fail to lead the market

485
00:39:05,176 --> 00:39:07,679
with our resources
and distribution network?

486
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:16,020
So you used investment as an excuse
to get our intel, in case you fail.

487
00:39:16,729 --> 00:39:19,691
I heard you've done that
with a few businesses with spies.

488
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:21,609
Spies?

489
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:24,904
Then what about Appello?

490
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:28,366
Do you think one of my people
is there or not?

491
00:40:09,991 --> 00:40:11,576
CEO Kang Ha-gi?

492
00:40:13,077 --> 00:40:15,371
I am Reporter Do Eun-yong
with Insight Business Newspaper.

493
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:18,666
INSIGHT BUSINESS NEWSPAPER
REPORTER DO EUN-YONG

494
00:40:19,167 --> 00:40:21,794
Nice to meet you. I look forward
to seeing great articles about us.

495
00:40:26,049 --> 00:40:29,260
Why don't you spare me some time?
I have many questions for you.

496
00:40:29,886 --> 00:40:31,970
Please contact my office
to schedule an interview.

497
00:40:31,971 --> 00:40:32,972
I don't mean Appello.

498
00:40:33,723 --> 00:40:34,766
I mean for you.

499
00:40:43,066 --> 00:40:45,025
I'm almost there. See you soon.

500
00:40:45,026 --> 00:40:46,486
I'm sorry. I must be somewhere.

501
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:49,447
Are you done?

502
00:41:06,339 --> 00:41:07,966
Why are you so dressed up?

503
00:41:08,633 --> 00:41:10,176
You're wearing perfume too.

504
00:41:10,510 --> 00:41:12,052
Stop getting clingy.

505
00:41:12,053 --> 00:41:14,722
Why? It's been so long
since we've met.

506
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:18,601
You only call me for business.

507
00:41:19,435 --> 00:41:21,646
Why are you staying at a hotel
and not at your place?

508
00:41:22,271 --> 00:41:23,398
Someone kept visiting me.

509
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:27,735
Be careful.
That can turn into an owner's risk.

510
00:41:28,111 --> 00:41:29,570
We're over already

511
00:41:29,779 --> 00:41:30,822
and it was an industry insider.

512
00:41:31,614 --> 00:41:33,116
You'd better keep that up.

513
00:41:34,951 --> 00:41:37,120
Only date someone
who has something to lose.

514
00:41:40,123 --> 00:41:43,209
I knew it.
That's the CEO Kang Ha-gi I know.

515
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:46,004
This is why
you haven't dated in a decade...

516
00:41:46,879 --> 00:41:49,506
Never mind. You were unable to date.

517
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:50,550
You're so cold-hearted.

518
00:41:51,009 --> 00:41:52,968
Find a hobby.

519
00:41:52,969 --> 00:41:54,345
Or start stanning a star.

520
00:41:55,722 --> 00:41:56,723
I already have a bias.

521
00:41:59,809 --> 00:42:01,728
You? Who?

522
00:42:03,479 --> 00:42:04,605
Appello.

523
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:06,691
I already know.

524
00:42:07,108 --> 00:42:09,193
You like me. Say it's me.

525
00:42:09,610 --> 00:42:11,069
Just say it's me.

526
00:42:11,070 --> 00:42:13,780
Say, "Lee Chan."
Say, "Lee Chan is my bias."

527
00:42:13,781 --> 00:42:15,867
- Appello.
- Lee Chan.

528
00:42:16,284 --> 00:42:17,993
- Appello.
- Lee Chan.

529
00:42:17,994 --> 00:42:19,411
- Appello.
- I'll bite you.

530
00:42:19,412 --> 00:42:20,872
I knew it.

531
00:42:43,061 --> 00:42:44,311
What's with her now?

532
00:42:44,312 --> 00:42:45,479
Let her be.

533
00:42:45,480 --> 00:42:48,232
Hey, Namda!
Come and eat some fried chicken!

534
00:42:48,649 --> 00:42:49,650
No!

535
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:52,153
I still have a long way to go!

536
00:42:59,619 --> 00:43:00,703
Hey, Mi-mi.

537
00:43:00,995 --> 00:43:04,372
Can I just do
a hundred of these again?

538
00:43:04,373 --> 00:43:07,376
I need to drain myself to forget
what happened at the CEO's office...

539
00:43:11,297 --> 00:43:12,506
It's coming back.

540
00:43:12,507 --> 00:43:15,134
You don't have to mind it.
Things like that happen in life.

541
00:43:15,676 --> 00:43:16,761
It can't.

542
00:43:18,346 --> 00:43:22,100
Guys, how am I going
to face the CEO from now on?

543
00:43:22,517 --> 00:43:24,894
And what about the entire company
thinking I'm a weird woman?

544
00:43:29,315 --> 00:43:30,690
It was only your first day.

545
00:43:30,691 --> 00:43:32,526
If you do your job well

546
00:43:32,527 --> 00:43:33,861
these rumors will die down quickly.

547
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:37,865
- Do you think so?
- Of course.

548
00:43:38,324 --> 00:43:40,408
And you're just a rookie.

549
00:43:40,409 --> 00:43:41,744
You won't have to meet the CEO often.

550
00:43:42,078 --> 00:43:43,204
Just avoid him.

551
00:43:44,539 --> 00:43:45,581
Right?

552
00:43:47,041 --> 00:43:50,670
I won't have to meet the CEO

553
00:43:51,337 --> 00:43:52,505
at all, right?

554
00:43:53,172 --> 00:43:54,882
- Not at all.
- Not likely.

555
00:43:56,175 --> 00:43:59,511
Right.
Yes, I doubt I'll have to see him.

556
00:43:59,512 --> 00:44:01,097
No, never again.

557
00:44:04,517 --> 00:44:06,686
I'll work hard
and improve my reputation.

558
00:44:07,061 --> 00:44:08,062
As for the CEO...

559
00:44:09,105 --> 00:44:10,273
I'll avoid him.

560
00:44:21,617 --> 00:44:23,994
It's our first pop-up store
since TUNZI's launch

561
00:44:23,995 --> 00:44:26,037
so please pay extra attention.

562
00:44:26,038 --> 00:44:27,039
- Yes.
- Yes, ma'am.

563
00:44:34,797 --> 00:44:38,092
TUNZI IS A SPACE
FOR DESIGNER MIN-JI'S...

564
00:44:47,977 --> 00:44:49,020
I'll do it!

565
00:44:59,572 --> 00:45:00,823
Let me help!

566
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:09,916
I'll take it!

567
00:45:24,639 --> 00:45:25,681
TUNZI OUTFIT SETTING LIST

568
00:45:50,623 --> 00:45:51,999
The doors are closing.

569
00:45:55,878 --> 00:45:57,170
Work hard.

570
00:45:57,171 --> 00:45:59,632
Avoid the CEO.

571
00:46:15,231 --> 00:46:16,399
The doors are closing.

572
00:46:19,819 --> 00:46:23,321
Hello, we're the rookie employees,
Nam Da-reum...

573
00:46:23,322 --> 00:46:25,240
- Park Young-woo...
- And Lee Min-a!

574
00:46:25,241 --> 00:46:26,575
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

575
00:46:28,286 --> 00:46:29,411
- Hello.
- How cute.

576
00:46:29,412 --> 00:46:31,329
- I love the energy.
- It's great to meet you.

577
00:46:31,330 --> 00:46:32,748
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

578
00:46:33,666 --> 00:46:35,418
- We'll do our best!
- We'll do our best!

579
00:46:36,419 --> 00:46:41,423
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

580
00:46:41,424 --> 00:46:44,093
- We'll do our best!
- We'll do our best!

581
00:46:45,636 --> 00:46:46,762
Thank you.

582
00:46:47,596 --> 00:46:49,265
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

583
00:47:13,789 --> 00:47:17,043
Here comes CEO Kang Ha-gi!

584
00:47:24,008 --> 00:47:25,051
Hello, Mr. Kang!

585
00:47:25,259 --> 00:47:27,345
- Hello, Mr. Kang!
- Hello, Mr. Kang!

586
00:47:27,553 --> 00:47:30,013
- Hello.
- Mr. Kang, please sit over here.

587
00:47:30,014 --> 00:47:32,641
Goodness, no. Why this table?

588
00:47:36,354 --> 00:47:37,396
Have a seat.

589
00:47:40,775 --> 00:47:42,525
I thought you'd be too busy to come.

590
00:47:42,526 --> 00:47:43,943
I have to leave soon

591
00:47:43,944 --> 00:47:45,528
for a video meeting
with a foreign VC firm.

592
00:47:45,529 --> 00:47:46,988
Mr. Kang, would you like a drink

593
00:47:46,989 --> 00:47:48,990
- I have a video meeting.
- Yes, right.

594
00:47:48,991 --> 00:47:50,826
- Can you pour me one?
- Have some.

595
00:47:53,037 --> 00:47:54,662
Why did the atmosphere turn gloomy?

596
00:47:54,663 --> 00:47:57,999
Everyone! Drink up. Come on.

597
00:47:58,000 --> 00:48:00,335
CEO Ha-gi is with us now

598
00:48:00,336 --> 00:48:03,254
so let's have a drink happily!
Drink up!

599
00:48:03,255 --> 00:48:04,799
- Drink up!
- Mr. Kang.

600
00:48:05,091 --> 00:48:06,425
Right. You aren't drinking.

601
00:48:06,884 --> 00:48:08,468
Please give us your guidance.

602
00:48:08,469 --> 00:48:10,054
We look forward to learning a lot.

603
00:48:14,433 --> 00:48:15,976
Let's call it a day quickly.

604
00:48:16,519 --> 00:48:17,937
Don't let the rookies get too drunk.

605
00:48:18,229 --> 00:48:19,271
Yes, sir.

606
00:48:22,900 --> 00:48:24,110
Let's keep drinking!

607
00:48:24,527 --> 00:48:26,987
Da-reum is at a company dinner,
and I'm really concerned.

608
00:48:27,780 --> 00:48:30,031
She'll chug every single drink
without turning anything down.

609
00:48:30,032 --> 00:48:31,534
She's a born nerd.

610
00:48:32,201 --> 00:48:33,828
That's the problem with Namda.

611
00:48:34,578 --> 00:48:36,872
She tries too hard.

612
00:48:50,428 --> 00:48:52,095
- Oh, wow.
- Manager, please have one.

613
00:48:52,096 --> 00:48:54,014
What? Me?

614
00:48:55,433 --> 00:48:57,767
Gosh, Da-reum. I didn't know
you were capable of this.

615
00:48:57,768 --> 00:48:59,519
I learned it from my friends.

616
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:02,231
You have great friends.
Wait a second, sweetie.

617
00:49:03,858 --> 00:49:05,025
You need a drink from me.

618
00:49:05,359 --> 00:49:06,402
Of course.

619
00:49:06,861 --> 00:49:08,737
- All right.
- Ms. Nam Da-reum.

620
00:49:09,321 --> 00:49:10,406
Sorry?

621
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:12,199
Take a drink from me instead.

622
00:49:13,868 --> 00:49:15,828
Right. Yes!

623
00:49:17,288 --> 00:49:18,622
Yes, right. Yes.

624
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:21,167
Use that glass.

625
00:49:21,750 --> 00:49:23,419
Right. Yes, sir!

626
00:49:24,295 --> 00:49:25,296
Okay.

627
00:49:26,630 --> 00:49:27,631
What?

628
00:49:31,343 --> 00:49:32,344
Team dinners are voluntary.

629
00:49:33,637 --> 00:49:34,930
If you're exhausted, you may go home.

630
00:49:37,641 --> 00:49:39,560
Yes, sir. I will.

631
00:50:06,962 --> 00:50:08,964
MEAT BARBECUE

632
00:50:10,841 --> 00:50:15,262
I should go for a quick recharge.

633
00:50:18,557 --> 00:50:20,434
- Drink up!
- Cheers!

634
00:50:21,852 --> 00:50:23,938
- Cheers!
- Have another drink.

635
00:50:24,355 --> 00:50:26,315
I have to be at a meeting soon,
so please excuse me.

636
00:50:26,607 --> 00:50:28,526
Yes, you should get going, Mr. Kang.

637
00:50:29,401 --> 00:50:31,111
Goodbye, Mr. Kang.

638
00:50:34,615 --> 00:50:35,699
Oh, okay.

639
00:50:37,743 --> 00:50:40,079
- I need some more.
- Come on!

640
00:50:52,424 --> 00:50:53,717
Why is Director Kim here?

641
00:51:07,314 --> 00:51:08,983
Darn it.

642
00:51:43,767 --> 00:51:47,104
If I work hard enough

643
00:51:47,605 --> 00:51:48,772
then one day

644
00:51:51,358 --> 00:51:54,820
I'll get to see you in person, right?

645
00:52:01,201 --> 00:52:04,747
Anyway, he looks really good
in this picture.

646
00:52:06,624 --> 00:52:09,460
I must take a picture.

647
00:52:15,633 --> 00:52:16,884
PASSCODE

648
00:52:17,843 --> 00:52:19,303
Why isn't it working?

649
00:52:20,304 --> 00:52:23,307
Zero. Nine. One. Six.

650
00:52:26,310 --> 00:52:28,937
That's Chan's birthday.

651
00:52:29,605 --> 00:52:33,901
Zero. Nine. One...

652
00:52:45,079 --> 00:52:46,080
Ms. Nam.

653
00:52:46,872 --> 00:52:47,915
Yes?

654
00:52:49,124 --> 00:52:50,668
What do you think you're doing here?

655
00:52:52,544 --> 00:52:53,753
Mr. Kang?

656
00:52:53,754 --> 00:52:55,339
Why are you here
in the middle of a company dinner?

657
00:52:55,756 --> 00:52:56,757
What?

658
00:52:57,216 --> 00:52:58,676
Me? You mean me?

659
00:52:59,218 --> 00:53:01,387
Oh, I...

660
00:53:01,595 --> 00:53:04,431
I needed to recharge for a bit.

661
00:53:05,099 --> 00:53:08,018
- Recharge?
- You said you always

662
00:53:09,061 --> 00:53:10,853
welcomed everyone

663
00:53:10,854 --> 00:53:12,356
and that your office

664
00:53:13,273 --> 00:53:15,651
was always open.

665
00:53:16,610 --> 00:53:19,405
So a picture.

666
00:53:20,030 --> 00:53:24,910
I was going to leave
after taking just one picture.

667
00:53:26,704 --> 00:53:27,705
What picture?

668
00:53:28,455 --> 00:53:29,456
A picture...

669
00:53:43,303 --> 00:53:46,140
Now, everyone. Attention, please.

670
00:53:46,932 --> 00:53:50,476
There is one question all rookies
of our company must answer.

671
00:53:50,477 --> 00:53:51,644
Yes, that one.

672
00:53:51,645 --> 00:53:54,230
Now, dear adorable Ms. Lee Min-a

673
00:53:54,231 --> 00:53:57,985
are you on Team Ha-gi or Team Chan?

674
00:53:59,069 --> 00:54:01,195
- What?
- Do you prefer someone like Mr. Kang

675
00:54:01,196 --> 00:54:02,905
who's very trustworthy

676
00:54:02,906 --> 00:54:04,824
and hard on the outside,
but soft on the inside?

677
00:54:04,825 --> 00:54:06,409
Or is it Director Chan

678
00:54:06,410 --> 00:54:08,495
someone unreal,
like he popped out of a fairy tale?

679
00:54:09,621 --> 00:54:11,748
Well, the thing is

680
00:54:11,749 --> 00:54:14,000
there's too much pressure.

681
00:54:14,001 --> 00:54:17,379
If they're too much pressure for you,
you can join Team Jin-sang.

682
00:54:18,005 --> 00:54:19,548
- Join me.
- What?

683
00:54:20,466 --> 00:54:22,425
- What?
- Come on. You ruined it.

684
00:54:22,426 --> 00:54:23,801
Hurry up and choose.

685
00:54:23,802 --> 00:54:25,721
In that case, I choose...

686
00:54:31,894 --> 00:54:34,188
Team Ha-gi.

687
00:54:35,564 --> 00:54:37,190
- I knew it.
- I was right.

688
00:54:37,191 --> 00:54:38,524
See? Me too.

689
00:54:38,525 --> 00:54:40,234
- Nice choice, Min-a.
- I was right.

690
00:54:40,235 --> 00:54:41,569
- I had a feeling.
- I'm on Team Ha-gi too!

691
00:54:41,570 --> 00:54:43,488
Why is everyone on Team Ha-gi?

692
00:54:43,489 --> 00:54:45,657
- Is anybody on Team Jin-sang?
- It's Ha-gi.

693
00:55:10,641 --> 00:55:13,227
Did she really break in
because she was just drunk?

694
00:56:28,051 --> 00:56:29,344
She didn't hear that, did she?

695
00:56:35,767 --> 00:56:36,768
Ms. Nam.

696
00:56:50,532 --> 00:56:52,075
Ms. Nam, time to go home.

697
00:56:52,743 --> 00:56:54,286
Wake up, Ms. Nam.

698
00:56:56,038 --> 00:56:58,206
What? Why?

699
00:57:10,719 --> 00:57:12,638
She's driving me insane.

700
00:57:14,890 --> 00:57:16,099
What now?

701
00:57:52,719 --> 00:57:53,887
I must be insane.

702
00:57:56,223 --> 00:57:57,557
I must be.

703
00:57:59,309 --> 00:58:00,644
Yes, I am.

704
00:58:04,398 --> 00:58:05,816
Oh, come on.

705
00:58:11,238 --> 00:58:12,698
I feel like throwing up.

706
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:25,460
What? You did it with the CEO...

707
00:58:29,673 --> 00:58:33,718
- You slept with him?
- What? No!

708
00:58:33,719 --> 00:58:37,097
I fell asleep in his office.

709
00:58:40,767 --> 00:58:42,978
I knew it. There's no way
our conservative girl would do that.

710
00:58:43,770 --> 00:58:45,230
So why did you go there?

711
00:58:47,566 --> 00:58:48,692
No idea.

712
00:58:49,192 --> 00:58:50,694
I guess
I was in my zombie mode again.

713
00:58:51,486 --> 00:58:53,487
There's a picture of Chan there.

714
00:58:53,488 --> 00:58:56,907
It's not a photoshoot, though.
It's such a candid picture.

715
00:58:56,908 --> 00:58:58,076
You're insane.

716
00:58:59,619 --> 00:59:01,704
You have to do something
about your drunken behavior.

717
00:59:01,705 --> 00:59:04,041
Da-reum,
you literally are killing me.

718
00:59:04,791 --> 00:59:08,045
I'm sorry.
I'll seriously quit drinking now.

719
00:59:08,378 --> 00:59:09,379
Jeez!

720
00:59:12,966 --> 00:59:15,469
Anyway, you didn't do
anything weird in the office, right?

721
00:59:15,969 --> 00:59:16,970
I

722
00:59:17,721 --> 00:59:18,972
hope not.

723
00:59:21,308 --> 00:59:23,184
What is this ominous feeling?

724
00:59:23,185 --> 00:59:25,187
- I don't know.
- Wait, no.

725
00:59:26,730 --> 00:59:27,856
Did you black out?

726
00:59:28,940 --> 00:59:29,983
Yes.

727
00:59:34,362 --> 00:59:35,780
Hey, Da-reum.

728
00:59:35,781 --> 00:59:38,283
- Hello.
- Oh, hello.

729
00:59:51,755 --> 00:59:53,965
Hey, Nam Da-reum!

730
00:59:54,966 --> 00:59:56,675
I saw a new side of you yesterday.

731
00:59:56,676 --> 00:59:58,886
You did something with this thing

732
00:59:58,887 --> 01:00:03,058
and bang, the bottle cap spun around,
flew over there, and blast!

733
01:00:04,726 --> 01:00:06,186
Gosh, you truly are different.

734
01:00:06,937 --> 01:00:08,355
- Give me five.
- What?

735
01:00:09,397 --> 01:00:12,275
M-Me? What did I do? Why...

736
01:00:15,070 --> 01:00:16,071
What's going on?

737
01:00:17,239 --> 01:00:19,115
You were so cool yesterday, Da-reum.

738
01:00:19,116 --> 01:00:20,283
You're the best, Da-reum.

739
01:00:31,962 --> 01:00:34,381
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

740
01:00:39,803 --> 01:00:41,011
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

741
01:00:41,012 --> 01:00:42,389
Did you get home safely last night?

742
01:00:42,597 --> 01:00:44,141
You seemed to have left
after getting drunk.

743
01:00:44,391 --> 01:00:45,934
Yes, I did.

744
01:00:54,109 --> 01:00:56,777
He's so good-looking.

745
01:00:56,778 --> 01:00:59,197
Ms. Nam.

746
01:01:00,574 --> 01:01:02,701
Wait, what is this memory?

747
01:01:03,243 --> 01:01:04,911
It feels like Mr. Kang was there.

748
01:01:06,121 --> 01:01:08,330
- Excuse me, Ms. Kim.
- Yes?

749
01:01:08,331 --> 01:01:11,667
By any chance, is Mr. Kang at work?

750
01:01:11,668 --> 01:01:12,752
Mr. Kang?

751
01:01:13,003 --> 01:01:14,796
I think
he spent the night up in his office.

752
01:01:15,172 --> 01:01:16,173
What?

753
01:01:23,972 --> 01:01:25,682
Darn it. What's going on?

754
01:01:25,891 --> 01:01:27,976
What happened?
Why is he looking at me?

755
01:01:28,310 --> 01:01:31,813
Please recall it.
Think hard, Nam Da-reum.

756
01:01:32,189 --> 01:01:34,274
SAMPLE ROOM

757
01:01:46,369 --> 01:01:48,371
I don't think I've sobered up yet.

758
01:01:48,830 --> 01:01:51,291
Da-reum! You were here?

759
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:53,376
- Do you feel okay?
- Yes.

760
01:01:54,628 --> 01:01:56,504
I got wasted last night, wasn't I?

761
01:01:56,796 --> 01:01:58,964
Did I make any mistakes?

762
01:01:58,965 --> 01:02:01,300
Mistakes? What mistakes?

763
01:02:01,301 --> 01:02:03,093
You left early,
so you didn't have time to do that.

764
01:02:03,094 --> 01:02:07,556
Da-reum, it would've been so much fun
if you stayed until the very end.

765
01:02:07,557 --> 01:02:10,476
At the end of the night,
Director Lee Chan came!

766
01:02:10,477 --> 01:02:12,103
He was so good-looking.

767
01:02:13,063 --> 01:02:14,105
What?

768
01:02:14,981 --> 01:02:16,190
My goodness.

769
01:02:16,191 --> 01:02:19,610
I thought he was just good-looking,
but he was hilarious too.

770
01:02:19,611 --> 01:02:20,903
- Yes.
- See?

771
01:02:20,904 --> 01:02:23,573
He only took a picture with us
to congratulate us on our start here!

772
01:02:28,328 --> 01:02:29,746
My Chan was there?

773
01:02:31,665 --> 01:02:36,085
You should call him
Director Lee at work.

774
01:02:36,086 --> 01:02:39,047
Shouldn't we call him that?

775
01:02:39,881 --> 01:02:43,176
Wait, Da-reum must've been
a fan of D.N.X.

776
01:02:43,468 --> 01:02:45,095
I almost said, "It's Lee Chan!"

777
01:02:45,804 --> 01:02:46,846
It could've been a mistake.

778
01:02:47,264 --> 01:02:48,265
Oh, no.

779
01:02:49,182 --> 01:02:50,684
What's wrong, Da-reum?

780
01:02:51,476 --> 01:02:53,019
Was it something I said?

781
01:02:56,481 --> 01:02:57,649
It's not that.

782
01:02:59,150 --> 01:03:00,277
It's nothing.

783
01:03:11,329 --> 01:03:12,706
Not only was I drunk

784
01:03:14,082 --> 01:03:16,251
but I broke into the CEO's office

785
01:03:18,795 --> 01:03:20,380
and didn't even get to see my Chan.

786
01:03:26,344 --> 01:03:28,263
Why are you even alive, Da-reum?

787
01:03:29,639 --> 01:03:31,474
Just end yourself.

788
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:36,730
That was my chance
to finally see him in person.

789
01:04:21,274 --> 01:04:22,275
Oh, mother!

790
01:04:25,653 --> 01:04:28,073
Why do you always look for your mom
whenever you see me?

791
01:04:29,491 --> 01:04:31,242
So, about yesterday...

792
01:04:33,995 --> 01:04:35,246
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

793
01:04:35,914 --> 01:04:38,958
I remember getting drunk
and walking into your office.

794
01:04:39,501 --> 01:04:41,544
But when I opened my eyes,
it was already morning.

795
01:04:44,923 --> 01:04:46,007
So you don't remember?

796
01:04:47,592 --> 01:04:49,844
How convenient.
You never remember anything.

797
01:04:51,179 --> 01:04:52,722
- Sorry?
- Forget it.

798
01:04:53,473 --> 01:04:54,599
It's better that way.

799
01:04:55,809 --> 01:04:57,226
I wanted to wake you
when you sobered up.

800
01:04:57,227 --> 01:04:59,229
But you were too drunk to do that.

801
01:04:59,521 --> 01:05:02,273
Then what about you?

802
01:05:05,443 --> 01:05:06,444
Well...

803
01:05:09,489 --> 01:05:10,490
I worked and left.

804
01:05:13,118 --> 01:05:15,245
Yes, right? I'm glad.

805
01:05:15,703 --> 01:05:17,162
I'm glad you didn't stay
because of me.

806
01:05:17,163 --> 01:05:18,372
Please be cautious from now on.

807
01:05:18,373 --> 01:05:19,416
That kind of behavior

808
01:05:20,250 --> 01:05:21,876
may cause
an unnecessary misunderstanding.

809
01:05:23,586 --> 01:05:24,587
Yes, sir.

810
01:05:25,004 --> 01:05:26,214
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

811
01:05:26,548 --> 01:05:28,258
I won't let
anything like this happen again.

812
01:05:30,301 --> 01:05:31,302
I'm sorry.

813
01:05:35,723 --> 01:05:37,349
- Yes, Ms. Kim.
- Hey, Da-reum.

814
01:05:37,350 --> 01:05:40,185
Go to the showroom on the first floor
and help out with organizing.

815
01:05:40,186 --> 01:05:41,396
Yes, coming.

816
01:05:43,022 --> 01:05:45,274
Ms. Kim needs me at the showroom

817
01:05:45,275 --> 01:05:46,985
so please excuse me.

818
01:05:56,786 --> 01:05:57,912
Ms. Nam.

819
01:06:02,500 --> 01:06:03,751
What? Why is he following me?

820
01:06:16,890 --> 01:06:19,267
The miracle I had always hoped for

821
01:06:21,144 --> 01:06:22,979
did not happen on a special day.

822
01:06:25,064 --> 01:06:27,942
It came into my trivial daily life

823
01:06:30,612 --> 01:06:33,573
in the least expected moment.

824
01:07:08,107 --> 01:07:11,694
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

825
01:07:22,747 --> 01:07:24,164
CHEON SEON-AE

826
01:07:24,165 --> 01:07:25,708
EPILOGUE

827
01:08:10,169 --> 01:08:12,754
Scrub with love

828
01:08:12,755 --> 01:08:16,175
Scrub the dirt off your heart

829
01:08:16,718 --> 01:08:20,178
Every corner, every grime

830
01:08:20,179 --> 01:08:22,724
Let me scrub it off for you

831
01:08:23,725 --> 01:08:27,686
Scrub, scrub with love

832
01:08:27,687 --> 01:08:31,024
The dirt on the bruise of your heart

833
01:08:31,274 --> 01:08:34,319
I will even scrub the bruises

834
01:08:34,694 --> 01:08:40,157
Of your heart with my love

835
01:08:40,158 --> 01:08:41,534
Scrub, scrub

836
01:08:41,951 --> 01:08:43,536
- Oh, my. Mr. Kang.
- Goodness.

837
01:08:44,495 --> 01:08:47,331
I mean,
it's a good morning, Ms. Cheon.

838
01:08:47,332 --> 01:08:49,416
Oh, no.
Did you spend the night up again?

839
01:08:49,417 --> 01:08:50,834
You should take a quick nap.

840
01:08:50,835 --> 01:08:52,462
I'll clean up quickly and leave.

841
01:08:57,425 --> 01:08:59,968
No, it's all right.

842
01:08:59,969 --> 01:09:01,386
My paperwork is all over the place.

843
01:09:01,387 --> 01:09:03,764
That's nothing new.

844
01:09:03,765 --> 01:09:05,682
It's not like
I've ever touched anything.

845
01:09:05,683 --> 01:09:07,643
If you have work to do, go ahead.

846
01:09:07,644 --> 01:09:09,103
I'll make it quick and leave.

847
01:09:11,898 --> 01:09:13,733
Ms. Cheon.

848
01:09:15,109 --> 01:09:16,861
Dear Ms. Cheon.

849
01:09:18,488 --> 01:09:19,489
Would you like

850
01:09:20,448 --> 01:09:21,741
to have a cup of coffee with me?

851
01:09:22,617 --> 01:09:25,787
Coffee? Morning coffee sounds great.

852
01:09:26,704 --> 01:09:30,208
Scrub, scrub, scrub the dirt

853
01:09:37,256 --> 01:09:39,342
- Nice to meet you, Da-reum.
- How do you know my name?

854
01:09:39,592 --> 01:09:40,927
I'm not dreaming, am I?

855
01:09:41,761 --> 01:09:43,429
Overseas training
for outstanding employees?

856
01:09:44,305 --> 01:09:46,640
I feel like she has a hidden agenda.

857
01:09:46,641 --> 01:09:48,725
Mr. Kang.

858
01:09:48,726 --> 01:09:50,603
You look so cool today.

859
01:09:50,978 --> 01:09:53,022
Maybe she's a honey trap

860
01:09:53,731 --> 01:09:54,857
Director Kim sent.

861
01:09:55,108 --> 01:09:57,360
- Call me.
- See you again!

862
01:09:58,861 --> 01:10:00,028
They're dating?

863
01:10:00,029 --> 01:10:01,947
Our company CEO and Chan?

864
01:10:01,948 --> 01:10:04,992
No!
